{"id":"rezin","name":"Rezin","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:rezin"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Rezin","text":"Firm; a prince, a king of Syria, who joined Pekah (q.v.) in an invasion of the kingdom of Judah (2 Kings 15:37; 16:5-9; Isa. 7:1-8). Ahaz induced Tiglath-pileser III. to attack Damascus, and this caused Rezin to withdraw for the purpose of defending his own kingdom. Damascus was taken, and Rezin was slain in battle by the Assyrian king, and his people carried into captivity, B.C. 732 (2 Kings 16:9)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7526","lemma":"רְצִין","xlit":"Rᵉtsîyn","gloss":"Retsin, the name of a Syrian and of an Israelite","kjv":"Rezin","count":11,"share":0.48},{"strong":"H7425","lemma":"רְמַלְיָהוּ","xlit":"Rᵉmalyâhûw","gloss":"Remaljah, an Israelite","kjv":"Remaliah","count":7,"share":0.3},{"strong":"H758","lemma":"אֲרָם","xlit":"ʼĂrâm","gloss":"Aram or Syria, and its inhabitants","kjv":"Aram, Mesopotamia, Syria, Syrians","count":9,"share":0.39},{"strong":"H271","lemma":"אָחָז","xlit":"ʼÂchâz","gloss":"Achaz, the name of a Jewish king and of an Israelite","kjv":"Ahaz","count":5,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H804","lemma":"אַשּׁוּר","xlit":"ʼAshshûwr","gloss":"Ashshur, the second son of Shem","kjv":"Asshur, Assur, Assyria, Assyrians. See H838","count":5,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H6492","lemma":"פֶּקַח","xlit":"Peqach","gloss":"Pekach, an Israelite king","kjv":"Pekah","count":3,"share":0.13}],"verses":["2Kgs.15.37","2Kgs.16.5","2Kgs.16.6","2Kgs.16.9","Ezra.2.48","Neh.7.50","Isa.7.1","Isa.7.4","Isa.7.8","Isa.8.6","Isa.9.11","2Kgs.16.7","2Kgs.16.8","Isa.7.2","Isa.7.3","Isa.7.5","Isa.7.6","Isa.7.7","Isa.7.9","Isa.8.4","Isa.8.5","Isa.8.7","Isa.8.8"],"related":[{"id":"pekah","type":"cooccur","shared":14,"jaccard":0.368,"why":"14 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"remaliah","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.143,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"tiglath-pileser","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":